{"id": "unknown-2026-05-05-005", "date": "2026-05-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 19, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["sustainable_textile", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Climate is now in the cost sheet", "content": "Climate risk is now embedded in apparel costs, not just ESG narratives.\nPolyester dominance ties the sector to fossil volatility, while emissions continue rising, led by tier 2 processing.\nCotton is becoming a weather premium, with supply shocks and imports influencing mill economics.\nRegulation, heat risks and carbon costs are turning sustainability into a core profitability lever.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/climate-is-now-in-the-cost-sheet-310098-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-05-006", "date": "2026-05-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 19, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "order_visibility", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["concerns", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "ICE cotton closes lower on profit booking at higher levels", "content": "ICE cotton futures fell after hitting contract highs, with July settling at 82.92 cents amid profit booking and long liquidation.\nWeak demand, rising certified stocks and lower trading volumes weighed on sentiment, while resistance near 84-85 cents capped gains despite support from a weaker dollar, firm crude oil and weather concerns in Texas.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-closes-lower-on-profit-booking-at-higher-levels-310100-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-05-007", "date": "2026-05-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 19, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam attracts $18.24 bn FDI in January-April 2026, trade up", "content": "Vietnam attracted $18.24 billion in FDI in January–April 2026, up 32 per cent, driven by manufacturing and processing. \nRealised FDI hit a five-year high, signalling continued capacity expansion. \nTrade surged to $344.17 billion, supported by strong US demand and rising imports from Asia, highlighting deeper global supply chain integration and export momentum.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-attracts-18-24-bn-fdi-in-january-april-2026-trade-up-310081-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-05-008", "date": "2026-05-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 19, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["optimistic", "growth", "decline", "slow", "weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam’s manufacturing growth weakens as costs surge in April", "content": "Vietnam’s manufacturing PMI fell to 50.5 in April 2026, signalling marginal growth and a seven-month low. \nNew orders declined for the first time in eight months, while input costs rose at a 15-year high due to fuel and logistics pressures. \nOutput growth slowed, employment and purchasing fell, and business sentiment weakened, though firms remained cautiously optimistic about future recovery. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-manufacturing-growth-weakens-as-costs-surge-in-april-310091-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-05-009", "date": "2026-05-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 19, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["[否定]increase", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "North India cotton yarn prices rise despite weak domestic demand", "content": "Rising cotton prices are driving sharp yarn price increases across North India, despite weak demand.\nSpinning mills hold pricing power, supported by strong exports and tight supply conditions.\nBuyers remain cautious, questioning the sustainability of current elevated price levels.\nCCI stock dynamics and limited arrivals are likely to keep cotton and yarn prices firm near term.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/north-india-cotton-yarn-prices-rise-despite-weak-domestic-demand-310088-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-05-010", "date": "2026-05-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 19, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["dominant", "growth", "decline", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s cumulative RMG exports down, but rebound in April", "content": "Bangladesh’s RMG exports saw a modest 2.82 per cent decline in FY26 (July–April), led by weaker knitwear.\nWoven garments showed relatively better resilience, while home textiles posted marginal growth.\nApril marked a sharp rebound, with strong YoY gains across apparel and home segments.\nDespite volatility, textiles remain dominant, contributing over 82 per cent of total exports.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-s-cumulative-rmg-exports-down-but-rebound-in-april-310079-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-05-011", "date": "2026-05-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 19, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US’ Carter’s taps retail veteran Sharon Price John as new CEO", "content": "Carter’s, Inc. appointed Sharon Price John as CEO & president effective June 15, 2026, succeeding Douglas C. Palladini. \nRichard F. Westenberger will serve as interim CEO. \nJohn, ex-Build-A-Bear Workshop chief, drove profitability, omnichannel growth and brand transformation; she also joins the board. \nCarter’s reaffirmed FY26 outlook, amid leadership transition and strategic reset. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-carter-s-taps-retail-veteran-sharon-price-john-as-new-ceo-310093-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-05-012", "date": "2026-05-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 19, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s $4 bn April rebound runs into the LDC clock", "content": "Bangladesh’s $4.01 billion garment exports in April (+33% YoY) is base-effect optics, with Eid-ul-Fitr 2025’s ten production-day shutdown flattering the comparison. \nThe real cliff is the November 2029 EBA expiry, not the 2026 LDC graduation; the WTO’s modelled hit is $5.37 billion, not the $8 billion figure Dhaka quotes. \nThe US zero-tariff carve-out is volume-quota, not cotton-content.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-s-4-bn-april-rebound-runs-into-the-ldc-clock-310086-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
